209:- **Q2.2** Which containers implement `Destroy`? — Exactly sixteen named Destroy impls: Array (T: Destroy); Heap, HeapArray and Vec (two each: T: Copy; T: Destroy); String (unconditional); Option (T: Destroy); Result (three: T: Destroy/E: Copy, T: Destroy/E: Destroy, T: Copy/E: Destroy); OrderedMap (four: each of K and V Copy or Destroy). HashMap excluded. <a id="q2-2-revision"></a>Revised 2026-11-06 by [information flow](#decided-project-infoflow-2026-11-06): `Secret<T>` is `Copy` only for scalar `T`; secret arrays and heap secrets are linear and their destruction wipes them.
